sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1 (--keep-items is record-only), R2-R4, swamp-vault-design. Same shape as tool.remove. docs/reference/vaultwarden.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: vault:teardown
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VW icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant VW as Vaultwarden<br/>vault.orbit Route
  CLI->>GW: vault:teardown<br/>--keep-items · --yes
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit vault:teardown --yes`
  %%> - syntax: `[--keep-items] [--yes] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Confirmation:
  %%> - in a terminal the CLI asks a default-No question; without a terminal, or with `--json`, `--yes` is required
  Note over GW: Validate, lock the vault<br/>task #5169 · 14 items
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the `vault` extension is on and Vaultwarden is set up, else `vault.not_configured`
  %%> - no other setup, sync or teardown runs, else `vault.sync_busy`
  %%> Decides:
  %%> - whether the published items must leave Vaultwarden, or only the setup goes
  alt with --keep-items
    Note over GW: Delete setup and ledger<br/>R1: no run, items stay
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the stored account, organization, collection and publishing ledger are deleted
    %%> - the items stay in Vaultwarden; a later setup on the same collection can adopt them
    %%> - no Swamp run starts (R1); Vaultwarden is not contacted
    GW-->>CLI: Torn down<br/>items kept in Vaultwarden
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the final result at once; there is nothing to follow
  else delete the items
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-vault-teardown
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - pushes the account secrets to the Swamp vault as `vault-teardown-5169` after commit (R3), then starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the setup and the ledger of published item IDs and sources, and the vault key names
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5169
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the task number, at once
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
    SW->>VW: Log in and unlock<br/>bw login · unlock · sync
    %%> How:
    %%> - the official Bitwarden CLI on 209, in a scratch home, trusting only the Orbit root CA
    SW->>VW: Read the collection<br/>bw list items
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - finds the items whose ID and decrypted `orbit.source` still match the ledger
    %%> Refuses:
    %%> - before any deletion, when a matching item also belongs to another visible collection: `vault.item_shared`
    SW->>VW: Delete the items<br/>bw delete --permanent
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - deletes each matching item permanently, one per step
    %%> Leaves:
    %%> - unrecorded copies and items whose source differs from the ledger
    SW->>VW: Log out<br/>bw logout · remove scratch home
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - logs out and deletes the scratch home, on success and on failure
    alt every item deleted
      VW-->>SW: 14 items deleted
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the deleted item IDs
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Delete setup and ledger<br/>task succeeded
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the stored account, organization, collection and publishing ledger are deleted
      %%> - task #5169 succeeds
    else a step fails
      VW--xSW: refused or no answer
      %%> When:
      %%> - login fails, Vaultwarden is down, an item is shared, or a delete fails
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      %%> The Gateway reads:
      %%> - which step failed and its safe error code
      Note over GW: Keep the setup<br/>ledger minus deleted items
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the setup stays; the ledger drops only the items that were deleted; task #5169 fails
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - safe: run the same command again; it deletes only what is still there
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show #5169
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
    end
  end
